{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793303219,"nonce":"5Qwg+qGLAsvkwPsG0xpOqB7/E2U=","title":"Step Pods mount the default service account token","message":"Found by an audit 2026-10-30: the k8s executor never sets automountServiceAccountToken: false on step Pods, so every Step can read /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token. A Step that runs PR code, or a value that reaches a program able to read files (curl -d @file), can send that token out. What it can do depends on the namespace's default ServiceAccount RBAC.\n\nFix: set automountServiceAccountToken: false on step and service Pods unless a Step needs the API (check the sidecar, workspace fetch and plugin Pods first; they may use their own tokens). Add a Pod-spec test.","files":null}]}